# App Store credentials — the committed TEMPLATE. Copy it to `native/.env`
# (gitignored, and kept out of the EAS upload by .easignore) and fill it in:
#
#   cp native/.env.example native/.env
#   make store-preflight            # says exactly what is still missing
#
# fastlane loads `.env` automatically — dotenv searches the `fastlane/` folder
# and its parent, and `bundle exec fastlane metadata` is run from `native/`, so
# this file is the parent. Nothing else reads it; `eas build` / `eas submit`
# take their identifiers from `eas.json` (see the bottom of this file), and the
# EAS CLI takes its own auth from `eas login` or EXPO_TOKEN.
#
# NONE of these values belong in the repo: the Apple Account email is personal
# data, the team ids are account-shaped, and the .p8 is a credential that can
# publish on your behalf. `native/*.p8` is gitignored too — keep the key file
# outside the tree anyway if you can.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Who fastlane is acting as (fastlane/Appfile reads all three).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Apple Account email the Apple Developer Program is under.
APPLE_ID=you@example.com

# Apple Developer Team ID — 10 alphanumerics. Developer portal → Membership,
# or the top-right team switcher in App Store Connect.
APPLE_TEAM_ID=ABCDE12345

# App Store Connect team id — fastlane's `itc_team_id`. A NUMBER, and a
# DIFFERENT thing from the 10-character id above.
#
# USUALLY LEAVE THIS BLANK. It only disambiguates an Apple Account that belongs
# to several App Store Connect teams, and only when authenticating by password:
# the API key below is issued BY one team, so it settles the team on its own.
# `make store-preflight` does not require it.
#
# If you do need it, it is NOT anywhere in the App Store Connect UI — Users and
# Access does not show it. Get it one of three ways:
#   • cd native && bundle exec fastlane spaceship
#     then, at the REPL:  Spaceship::Tunes.select_team
#   • logged in to App Store Connect, open this in the same browser and read
#     `contentProviderId` out of the JSON:
#     https://appstoreconnect.apple.com/WebObjects/iTunesConnect.woa/ra/user/detail
#   • ~/.fastlane/spaceship/<apple-id>/ — cached after any fastlane run
# ASC_TEAM_ID=123456789

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App Store Connect API key. Preferred over an Apple ID password because a .p8
# carries no 2FA session to expire halfway through an upload.
#
# App Store Connect → Users and Access → Integrations → App Store Connect API
# → generate a key with the **App Manager** role. The .p8 downloads ONCE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The key's own id (the `AuthKey_<KEY_ID>.p8` filename carries it).
ASC_KEY_ID=XXXXXXXXXX

# Issuer ID — one per team, shown above the key list. A UUID.
ASC_ISSUER_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Where the .p8 lives. Absolute, or relative to `native/` (fastlane runs there).
ASC_KEY_PATH=/absolute/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
# …or, instead of a path, the key file base64-encoded — for CI, where there is
# no filesystem to put it on. Set ONE of the two, never both.
# ASC_KEY_CONTENT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAS. Only needed to drive builds non-interactively (CI does this with the
# EXPO_TOKEN repo secret); a laptop uses `eas login` instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# EXPO_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-time escape hatches. Both are for LOCAL builds only — a store build
# must set neither. Left commented out on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Drops the iCloud + Game Center entitlements so a build signs on an Apple ID
# that has neither capability enabled. Cloud save, achievements and
# leaderboards all report themselves unavailable. See native/README.md.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CLOUD_SAVE=off

# Points the WebView at a deployed slot instead of the copy of the game bundled
# inside the app. Debugging only: a store build that streams the website is the
# exact shape App Store guideline 4.2 rejects.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GAME_URL=https://game.niclaslindstedt.se/preview/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT here, deliberately: the app's numeric Apple ID (`ascAppId`) and the team
# id EAS submits with. Those go in `eas.json` → submit.production.ios, because
# eas.json is read by the EAS CLI and does not expand environment variables.
# Both are public anyway — the numeric id is the `id######` in the App Store
# URL — so committing them is fine. `make store-preflight` checks they're set.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
